    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "can u help me compare the thermal dissipation rates of ceramic vs semi-metallic brake pads? looking at high-speed deceleration scenarios specifically. also interested in how heat soak affects the friction coefficient over repeated cycles.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Ceramic and semi-metallic brake pads have different thermal dissipation profiles, which is crucial in high-speed deceleration. Generally, ceramic pads tend to operate at slightly lower temperatures and have a more consistent friction coefficient across a wide range, which is good for predictable stopping power. Semi-metallic pads, while often providing higher initial bite, can sometimes experience more aggressive heat buildup, which can lead to noticeable changes—or \"fade\"—in the friction coefficient during repeated high-stress cycles. The heat soak effect, where residual heat affects performance between stops, is a major factor, and the material composition dictates how quickly that heat dissipates into the caliper and rotor.",
      "source": "target",
